WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
From a cabinet IR to a GT-100 patch
A WAV supplies the target frequency response. Pseudo IR finds cabinet and EQ settings the GT-100 can run on its own.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Search complete cabinet configurations
The fixed library contains 7 cabinets × 5 microphones × 2 axes × 11 positions. Each complete combination gets a volume-aligned score.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Include CUSTOM cabinets and Color
CUSTOM adds speaker size, speaker count and cabinet character. Low and High Color are experimental magnitude predictions, not new recordings.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Expanded Color + EQ search
Several promising bases are refined. CUSTOM Color and EQ are alternated, then the lowest full-band error with EQ + 2 FX selects one base for all four versions.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Compare both EQ fitting priorities
80 Hz–6 kHz and a focused 200 Hz–5 kHz strategy are tested. Auto chooses the lower full-band RMS at each level; Nerd Mode can compare either strategy.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Start with the dedicated EQ
Shelves, two parametric mid bands and low/high cuts reshape the cabinet response. Only settings available on the GT-100 are used.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Add one FX, or use both
One FX can be parametric or graphic. With two FX, the search compares P + P, P + G and G + P. All active EQs can be readjusted together.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Choose the physical block order
P means parametric; G means graphic. The dedicated EQ is P. Mixed chains test P > G > P, P > P > G and G > P > P, favoring lower intermediate gain.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:30.000
See what each EQ contributes
Nerd Mode shows each block separately, including its LEVEL. Zero dB means no change; positive values boost and negative values cut.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Choose your resource budget
All four versions share the selected cabinet. More EQ blocks may improve the match, but occupy effects you could otherwise use in your patch.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Prepare and compare guitar previews
Connect the GT-100 and choose Preamp A or B. Prepare preview records the available guitar samples through that preamp, restores the patch, then enables comparison.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Read the scores, then trust your ears
Proximity measures volume-aligned spectral shape. A waveform null test is a separate, phase-sensitive audio diagnostic; it does not rank cabinet candidates.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:44.000
Apply the version you want to keep
Choose the version, FX1 or FX2 when using one FX, and Preamp A or B. Apply updates the temporary patch. Use WRITE to keep it in the GT-100.
